# Copy this file to .env (never commit .env) before running `docker compose build`.

# HOST_UID / HOST_GID: NOT arbitrary values. They are the numeric ids of YOUR user and group on
# this machine, so the files the containers write to ./data and ./manifests belong to you.
# Get them with `id -u` (HOST_UID) and `id -g` (HOST_GID); on a single-user Linux PC both are
# usually 1000. Or let a command fill them (see the root README, "Guia de execução", Passo 2):
#   [ -f .env ] || printf 'HOST_UID=%s\nHOST_GID=%s\nHF_TOKEN=\n' "$(id -u)" "$(id -g)" > .env
# Also run `mkdir -p data` once: if ./data does not exist, Docker creates it as root and the
# `app` service cannot write to it.
HOST_UID=1000
HOST_GID=1000

# Optional: the code_contests dataset is public, so a token is not required.
# It only raises the Hugging Face rate limits.
HF_TOKEN=

# Local model (Qwen2.5-Coder-14B via Ollama), used only by `python -m ai_clients generate`.
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL: address of the Ollama server. For Ollama running on THIS machine use
#   http://host.docker.internal:11434 (the `app` service maps that name to the host);
#   for a remote server use http://<server>:11434; behind a tunnel (cloudflared or ngrok) use the
#   tunnel's https:// address (a quick-tunnel address changes every time the tunnel restarts).
#   With two Ollama servers, each `generate --resume` gets its own `-e OLLAMA_BASE_URL=...`
#   (see src/ai_clients/README.md); the value here is only the default. Never commit tunnel URLs.
# OLLAMA_HARDWARE_LABEL: free text describing the machine where Ollama runs (GPU, CPU, RAM), for
#   example "RTX 3060 12GB, Ryzen 5 5600". Written as-is next to every answer of the model; it is
#   never detected automatically (Ollama may run on another machine). With two Ollama servers,
#   both `generate` use this same label.
OLLAMA_BASE_URL=
OLLAMA_HARDWARE_LABEL=

# Optional. OLLAMA_HTTP_TIMEOUT_S: the longest wait without receiving anything from Ollama (default
# 900; the answer is streamed, so a long answer that keeps arriving is never cut; raise it if Ollama
# runs on CPU). OLLAMA_MAX_INFRA_RETRIES: how many consecutive times the same call is retried when
# Ollama is unreachable before the command stops (default 30). Neither changes any answer.
# OLLAMA_HTTP_TIMEOUT_S=900
# OLLAMA_MAX_INFRA_RETRIES=30

# Optional. OLLAMA_MODEL: leave it unset. The model of the experiment is qwen2.5-coder:14b (the
# default); this variable exists only for a pilot that compares models. Another model must be
# installed (`ollama pull <model>`), and since a run records its model and `--resume` refuses
# another one, changing it means a new run in an empty data/suites/slm.
# The seed and the temperature of each attempt are fixed by the attempt policy, not set here.
# OLLAMA_MODEL=qwen2.5-coder:14b

# Commercial models (GPT-5.4-mini, Gemini 3.8 Flash and Claude Haiku 5.5), used only by
# `python -m ai_clients generate --model gpt|gemini|claude`. Keys of accounts with billing enabled:
# on the free tier of the Gemini API the content may be used to improve Google's products. A model
# whose key is empty does not run; the others run normally. The dry run needs no key.
# Not needed to USE the packaged results (data/*.zip): only HOST_UID and HOST_GID are.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional. How many calls run at the same time in one `generate` (default 4), how many consecutive
# times the same call is retried when the API is unreachable or rate limited before the command
# stops (default 30), and the longest wait for one answer, in seconds (default 900; the answer only
# arrives after the whole reasoning). None of them changes any answer.
# OPENAI_MAX_CONCURRENCY=4
# GEMINI_MAX_CONCURRENCY=4
# ANTHROPIC_MAX_CONCURRENCY=4
# OPENAI_MAX_INFRA_RETRIES=30
# GEMINI_MAX_INFRA_RETRIES=30
# ANTHROPIC_MAX_INFRA_RETRIES=30
# LLM_HTTP_TIMEOUT_S=900
# Optional. At most this many requests START per minute, retries included, spread evenly (unset:
# no pacing). Use the limit of your plan: on the free tier of the Gemini API, 5 per minute (set
# also GEMINI_MAX_CONCURRENCY=1). A daily quota that runs out stops the command (code 3): run it
# again with --resume after the quota resets.
# OPENAI_MAX_REQUESTS_PER_MINUTE=
# GEMINI_MAX_REQUESTS_PER_MINUTE=5
# ANTHROPIC_MAX_REQUESTS_PER_MINUTE=
